meta {
  name: Add player
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/players
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  name: {{playerName}}
  myclub-id: {{myClubId}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  myClubId: 123
  playerName: 
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("redirects to the player list on success", function() {
    expect(res.getHeader("hx-redirect")).to.equal("/players");
  });
}

docs {
  Success is `HX-Redirect: /players` with an empty body. Every validation
  failure returns the re-rendered form instead, also as `200`.
  
  New players get run power and ball handling 5, and `is_goalie = false`.
  
  Bump `myClubId` in the environment between successful runs, or you hit
  the duplicate check.
  
  ## Edge cases
  
  | Change | Expected |
  |---|---|
  | `name` empty or only spaces | "Name can't be empty." — the check trims first |
  | `myclub-id: not-a-number` | "MyClub ID must be a number, like 1337." |
  | `myclub-id` empty | see the bug below |
  | `myclub-id` already used | "Player with this MyClub ID already exists." |
  | `myclub-id: -5` | ACCEPTED and written to the DB |
  | `myclub-id: 9223372036854775808` | rejected — one past int64, the parse fails |
  | both fields empty | two field errors at once |
  
  The UI form is `type="number"` with `min="0"`, so the non-numeric and
  negative cases are only reachable from here.
  
  ## Two things to watch on those
  
  1. Empty `myclub-id` reports the WRONG message. The empty check sets
     "MyClub ID can't be empty.", then `ParseInt("")` fails and overwrites
     it with "must be a number" — same map key, second write wins. The
     user is told the field is malformed when it's actually blank.
  
  2. Watch the server log on the non-numeric case. The log line has a
     broken format verb (`%\n` instead of `%v`) in
     cmd/web/handlers_players.go, so it prints `%!(NOVERB)`.
  
  On the negative case, the handler only checks that the value parses as
  an integer — there's no range check, so `-5` is stored as-is.
}
